From 778bc860e5a72d05427cf47496e201d5fe8f02c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:43:01 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] video-stream: raise the frame rate ceiling to 60

A new stream's input frame rate is estimated from the frames that led
to its creation, and that estimate is capped at MAX_FPS, 30. The
GStreamer encoder takes it as the source frame rate: it is the
framerate in the appsrc caps, which are set once for the stream's
size, and it sizes the stream's maximum bit rate, the frame period
used for drop decisions and the playback margin. So a source drawing
at 60 frames per second gets an encoder configured for 30 for the life
of the stream, even though the estimate itself is re-measured without
any cap every RED_STREAM_INPUT_FPS_TIMEOUT.

Raise MAX_FPS to 60, which is what common displays refresh at and what
hardware encoders handle. Sources at 30 frames per second or less are
unaffected, since the estimate only reaches the cap when frames arrive
faster than it.

The GL draw stream already started at 60, written as MAX_FPS * 2 with
a comment saying 60 is the upper bound for a hardware encoder. Write
it as MAX_FPS, so it stays at 60 rather than doubling with the new
ceiling.

The builtin MJPEG encoder keeps its own ceiling, MJPEG_MAX_FPS, 25,
which its quality and frame rate trade-off is tuned around, so MJPEG
streams still send at most 25 frames per second.
SPICE_GST_DEFAULT_FPS stays at 30 too: it is the rate GStreamer
encoders assume when there is no estimate at all, not a ceiling.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 server/video-stream.cpp | 2 +-
 server/video-stream.h   | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/server/video-stream.cpp b/server/video-stream.cpp
index 5aa7cbe5..1c24a2bf 100644
--- a/server/video-stream.cpp
+++ b/server/video-stream.cpp
@@ -487,7 +487,7 @@ bool display_channel_create_gl_draw_stream(DisplayChannel *display)
     /* This is the upper bound; it should be possible to stream at 60 FPS
      * with a hardware based encoder.
      */
-    stream->input_fps = MAX_FPS * 2;
+    stream->input_fps = MAX_FPS;
 
     display->priv->gl_draw_stream = stream;
     FOREACH_DCC(display, dcc) {
diff --git a/server/video-stream.h b/server/video-stream.h
index 5c71556b..25c1a740 100644
--- a/server/video-stream.h
+++ b/server/video-stream.h
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@
 #define RED_STREAM_CLIENT_REPORT_TIMEOUT MSEC_PER_SEC
 #define RED_STREAM_DEFAULT_HIGH_START_BIT_RATE (10 * 1024 * 1024) // 10Mbps
 #define RED_STREAM_DEFAULT_LOW_START_BIT_RATE (2.5 * 1024 * 1024) // 2.5Mbps
-#define MAX_FPS 30
+#define MAX_FPS 60
 
 struct VideoStream;
 
